& [SourcePreservation]
  + raw source is separately retained by exact byte length and SHA256 and is not rewritten by this review
  + the user intent to make SOP meaning compactly callable is preserved while a digest-only reconstruction claim is refused

& [Delineation]
  + Slice7 owns lifecycle semantic replay
  + Slice8 owns stateless MCP transport
  + Slice9 owns a pure immutable request-to-handle-to-retained-request relation
  + a future host owns mutation concurrency lifetime persistence eviction and authorization

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [keys] request_digest
  + [identities] handle entry registry request_id operation root_digest
  + [relations] handle commits request entry retains both registry orders entries resolve returns retained request validation delegates to Slice7
  + [bounds] eight entries eight megabytes per normalized request sixty-four megabytes aggregate retained request bytes
  + [invariants] exact profiles strict JSON canonical digest keys exact counts exact retained-byte sum whole-entry root replay fixed nonclaims

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] later MCP calls can send one compact handle and the host can retain large proof lineages without repeatedly occupying model-visible arguments
  + [convergent] P0 is a pure value with no hidden global registry persistence expiry eviction network filesystem or authorization

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + [identity] handle entry and registry are non-substitutable and profile-versioned
  + [content] the entry owns the exact normalized typed request rather than only its hash
  + [order] BTreeMap digest order makes roots independent of insertion order
  + [bounds] entry and aggregate bytes are recomputed before successor publication
  + [honesty] resolution states retained replay and never hash reconstruction
  + [security] every lookup validates the whole registry then exact handle equality and entry-to-request binding
  + [growth] a mutable MCP wrapper remains separately sourced

& [PruningTrace]
  + pruned adding state to cantor-compiler-mcp because Slice8 is canonically stateless
  + pruned filesystem or database persistence because it introduces freshness recovery and authorization duties
  + pruned storing validation responses because responses can be deterministically regenerated and would create stale duplicate state
  + pruned rejecting semantically refused requests because exact custody is useful for diagnosis and must not reclassify Slice7 outcomes
  + pruned hash-only lookup because omitted semantic bytes cannot be reconstructed from a digest

